okens":182.22222222222223,"requests":1},"project.symbol-reference-completeness":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":119867.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":2625.0,"requests":4}}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a concrete check that contracts.py, the schema, and the prompt enumerate the identical two `kind` values (e.g. an enum in the schema, or a unit test asserting the value sets match) so AC2 has proving evidence rather than prose.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5d","T5e"],"criteria":["E6","T4"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'The kind field is an unconstrained \"type\": \"string\" with no enum, so a mismatch fails SILENTLY rather than raising.'","AC2: 'contracts.py and the JSON schema describe the same two values.'"],"finding":"AC2 ('contracts.py and the JSON schema describe the same two values') has no concrete proving command; the plan itself notes the kind field is an unconstrained string with no enum, so nothing enforces that the schema and contracts agree — a mismatch fails silently.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb888095ff2ef1fb3","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria / Ordering constraint","norm_id":"nd305066924046239","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future edit changes one of the two values in contracts.py but not the schema (or the prompt), and no check catches the drift."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add `\"enum\": [\"codebase-verifiable\", \"non-codebase\"]` (allowing legacy value only in the reader per S2) or a unit test that imports the contract constants and asserts they equal the schema's stated values.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on