":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"After S2 is deployed and both values are accepted, tighten the JSON schema `kind` to an enum of the supported values; in the interim, have the audit reader emit a warning log when it encounters a kind it does not recognize.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json` (the `acceptance_items_classified` / `evidence_kind_matches_tag` classification vocabulary) in the edit set — or state explicitly why it needs no change — since it is an LLM-facing consumer that a held-out edge test requires to match the emitted `kind`.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan 'What' names only src/rebar/llm/contracts.py:116, src/rebar/schemas/completion_verdict.schema.json:26,49, and src/rebar/llm/reviewers/completion_verifier.md:224","criteria_routing.json:1241 'acceptance_items_classified': 'Classify the completion evidence as codebase-verifiable, non-codebase ...'","tests/unit/test_kind_wire_value_cutover_edge.py:61 test_registry_classification_vocabulary_matches_the_emitted_value asserts the routing check must match the emitted value: 'If it still says operator-attested while the verifier emits non-codebase, the two LLM-facing contracts disagree and the mismatch is unobservable at runtime.'"],"finding":"The emitted `kind` value has a co-equal LLM-facing consumer the edit set does not enumerate: `criteria_routing.json`'s `acceptance_items_classified` (and `evidence_kind_matches_tag`) classification check tells the model the vocabulary to classify criteria into. If it names a different token family than the verifier emits, the two LLM-facing contracts disagree with no runtime signal (kind has no enum). A held-out edge test asserts exactly this agreement, yet the plan's 'What' section lists only contracts.py, the schema, and completion_verifier.md.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f923a5aa5b640543a","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"What section (edit-set enumeration)","norm_id":"n9226b0bc06209a5c","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The verifier emits `non-codebase` but the classification prompt still instructs the model to classify into `operator-attested`, producing silently inconsistent LLM-facing vocabulary with no schema/test failure on the emit path itself."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add criteria_routing.json to the 'What' section's edit list (or a 'consumers verified unchanged' note) confirming its classification vocabulary names `codebase-verifiable`/`non-codebase` in lockstep with the emitter.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no